  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 211 AM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nThrough early next week...\n\nRidge dominance will maintain a summer regime through the period \nwhich will continue to support heat advisory criteria this week. An \nareawide heat advisory is in effect today through 7 PM. Heat \nadvisories will likely be needed throughout the rest of the week as \nwell, but with convection forecast, this will have to be assessed \nday to day. A plume of rich moisture associated with a disturbance \nrounding the southern flank of the ridge from the east will provide \nan environment for efficient rainfall, so localized flash flooding \ncannot be ruled out within any convective storms. The biggest \nopportunity for heavy rainfall looks to be Friday where vectors \nfavor slow storm motions and backbuilding. The coverage of \nconvection however is a little uncertain. Given the environment, \nhave decided to introduce a limited hazard graphic at this time. \nRain chances will continue as the ridge weakens into the weekend \ninto early next week. This should provide relief from the heat. \n/SAS/",
